{
 "frame": "chair frame, mm: +X chair's right, +Y forward, +Z up, table top Z=0. Stations y along each arm (same y as parts/arms.json).",
 "what": "The arms' thickness and underside (parts/arms.json gives only their top). h_outer(y) = how far the OUTER bottom arris sits straight below the arm's outer top arris; h_inner(y) = how far the INNER bottom arris sits below that same outer top arris. The underside is the straight line across between the two (no crease is seen across it). Thickness 'vertical' is h; 'square' is square to the top line in side view (h x cos of the top's slope; the arm rises 14-23 degrees toward the front).",
 "method": "tools/arm_underside/ (strip -> snap -> solve -> fit). Each arm's outer side face is unrolled in every photo that sees it onto the vertical surface through that arm's own outer top arris (strip.py); the top arris and the bottom arris(es) are seeded by eye and snapped to the tone edge (snap.py); every photo's bottom line is registered on its OWN top-arris trace, so each drop is measured within one photo; all photos are then solved together for the drop h(y) and the inboard offset a(y) of the line (solve.py; Legendre polynomials, Huber 0.6 mm; photos from above and below separate the two). Jackknife over photos gives se. Inputs (seeds, snapped traces, trusted ranges): tools/arm_underside/inputs/.",
